content.content:
{
  "fields": {
    "schema-version": "2"
  },
  "item-count": 1,
  "schema-version": 2,
  "sections": {
    "releases": [
      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "category": "added",
            "id": "added",
            "notes": "- `POST /samples`, `GET /series`, and `GET /summary/<series>` HTTP endpoints for ingesting samples and reading back per-series summaries.\n- Line-based sample ingest format (`<series> <value> [<at>]`), buffered through a bounded queue; under sustained overload the queue drops the oldest buffered samples rather than refusing new ones, so the recent window keeps advancing.\n- Per-series in-memory sample storage, kept time-sorted, with a configurable cap per series (oldest evicted on overflow).\n- Fixed-width windowed rollups (count/sum/min/max per window) and a summary rollup (overall count/mean/min/max plus covered time span) over a series' retention window.\n- Sample validation on ingest — series name pattern, finite numeric value, non-negative timestamp — with a rejection that names the offending field.\n- Runtime configuration via environment variables (`ROLLUP_WINDOW_MS`, `ROLLUP_MAX_SAMPLES`, `ROLLUP_RETENTION_MS`), validated at startup rather than silently ignored."
          }
        ],
        "date": "2026-09-04",
        "id": "0-3-0",
        "title": "0.3.0"
